WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/charts/ChartExportMenu.tsx — a PURE presentational leaf (no data hooks; the prompt's
  "Data sources" are only useOptionalToast + useTranslation). A single Download-glyph trigger (ghost icon
  Button) opens a dropdown <div role="menu"> of export actions:
      [optional] "Download data as CSV"  (FileSpreadsheet)  — present only when onExportCsv supplied; NOT busy-gated
                 "Save as PNG"            (Image)            — disabled while `busy`
                 "Save as SVG"            (FileImage)        — disabled while `busy`
                 "Copy image to clipboard"(Copy)             — disabled while `busy`; awaits a ClipboardOutcome
  Trigger `disabled` while the chart is loading/empty → aria-label "Chart not ready to export" (cannot open);
  otherwise "Export chart". onCopyImage resolves to ClipboardOutcome and announces via useOptionalToast:
      'copied'   → toast.success("Chart image copied to clipboard")
      'fallback' → toast.info("Clipboard not available — image downloaded instead")
      'failed'   → toast.error("Failed to copy chart image")
  useOptionalToast() returns null outside a <ToastProvider> → the menu degrades gracefully (no toast).
  No loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches of its own — those belong to the chart container it embeds in
  (identical contract to the ToolCard precedent, p4-apple-feature-views-0010).

