PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform idioms; no Tailwind ported)
  hand-rolled dropdown (absolute panel + outside-click/Escape useEffect) → SwiftUI `Menu` (HIG analogue: gets
        dismissal, keyboard nav, focus, and aria-haspopup/aria-expanded VoiceOver semantics for free).
  @/components/ui/Button (ghost icon trigger) → the Menu label, styled with the ghost design tokens
        (square.and.arrow.down glyph, Color.TS.textSecondary/textMuted, 28×28 hit target — web !h-7 !w-7).
  Lucide FileSpreadsheet/Image/FileImage/Copy → SF Symbols tablecells / photo / doc.richtext / doc.on.clipboard.
  @/components/feedback/Toast via useOptionalToast → ChartExportToastPresenter (optional; nil == web no-provider
        no-op) + the shipped @Observable center & ChartExportToastOverlay so the toast surface actually renders.
  useTranslation t(key, default) → ChartExportMenuStrings.string(key, fallback) (NSLocalizedString, table
        "ChartExportMenu") — every label/message/role resolves through the facade; zero English literals in code.
  i18n keys (verbatim from source): chart.export.{disabledTooltip,menuLabel,copySuccess,copyFallback,copyFailed,
        csv,png,svg,copy} — all present in ChartExportMenu.strings with their web English values.
  a11y      : trigger carries the contextual label ("Export chart" / "Chart not ready to export"); each item is a
        Label(title+symbol) so VoiceOver speaks it; busy/disabled items get the disabled trait; the toast chip
        merges into one announcement prefixed with its severity role; decorative icons are .accessibilityHidden.
        Reduce Motion honored (toast cross-fades instead of sliding). Dynamic Type via system fonts/tokens.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="ChartExportMenu" via ChartExportMenuSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11), default
        OSLog sink, fired from the view's `.task`.

