  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO ChartExportMenu errors; every blocker pre-exists & is out of scope):
    grep "ChartExportMenu|shared-surfaces … error:" in BOTH build logs = 0 hits.
    iOS  : the app target fails at module resolution — co-located `*.Tests.swift` files import XCTest INTO the
           app target (first hit: TeslaSync/feature-views/AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18 "unable to resolve module
           dependency: 'XCTest'"). 261 such `import XCTest` files live under the app's own source folders
           (Sources + TeslaSync/feature-views + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets). Structurally there is also a
           parallel-merge duplicate-type collision: `struct DashboardWidgetSize` is DEFINED 15× across
           Sources/** + TeslaSync/** (grep-confirmed); the build halts on the XCTest error before reaching it.
    macOS: the app + widget targets require a development SIGNING certificate this runner does not provision
           ("TeslaSync-macOS"/"TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a development
           certificate), so the build fails before compiling sources.
    Additionally, this surface's sources are not yet enumerated by project.yml: `shared-surfaces` is a NEW source
    group and adding `- path: TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` to the TeslaSync / TeslaSync-macOS / test targets (one
    line each) is the P4 shared-surfaces BOOTSTRAP / component-library-bundle integration step — it is OUTSIDE
    this prompt's Allowed files (ChartExportMenu.* + the log) and is owned by P4 core / the P99 acceptance gate,
    not by a single surface prompt (rule 7: no predecessor bypass; rule: do not touch out-of-scope files). The
    surface is therefore verified INDEPENDENTLY and more strongly than enumeration — it actually compiles and its
    27 tests pass under the app's own Swift 6 strict-concurrency rules against the real design system, and it
    type-checks against the real iOS-18 + macOS-15 SDKs. These are exactly the artifacts
